  "description": "RUHGIN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H168 N4 O4 Si8 Sm4,2(C5 H12). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 3 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 3 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 3 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.411-3.475 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.37-102.23°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C72H167N4O4Si8Sm4·(C5H12)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
